# Weight profile flashnext-unc-4.05: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Uncensored (orcarouter's abliterated build of
# Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) in Lygodactylus's EXL3 4.05 bpw pack (the HF repo below at the pinned commit,
# ~109.1 GB with its n-gram table), its own MTP draft layer, the table cold. The table is read past the
# page cache.
# The pack as published does not load: its vision tower is unquantized (16-bit) with a pre-fused qkv, and
# the loader builds the tower from EXL3 blocks (engine/models/flashnext/vision.py). Quantize the tower
# with tools/fn_tower_quantize.py and put the sidecar it writes, vision_tower_exl3.safetensors, in the
# pack folder: the loader reads it through its vision_*.safetensors rule
# (engine/models/flashnext/pack.py). Without the sidecar the switch fails at the tower load and
# ops/use-profile.sh rolls back. No QSE_FN_VISION_FILE: the pack has no vision_k6.safetensors (its
# tower is in the shards, the sidecar beside them).
# Switch with ops/use-profile.sh flashnext-unc-4.05.
QSE_FN_BPW=unc-4.05
QSE_WEIGHTS_REVISION=9c715c0b1a745b7db1c335347e8d45595b3cad3a
QSE_WEIGHTS_GB=109.1
QSE_FN_TABLE=cold
# MemAvailable (GiB) a start needs: the built-in flashnext-4.05 profile's numbers, unchanged (this
# pack's weights measured 63.88 GiB on the device at load, against the built-in pack's 62.47;
# vision 0.27 GiB).
QSE_MEM_NEED_GIB=85
# SRV-335: the engine's limits, the built-in flashnext-4.05 profile's.
MEM_CEILING_GIB=81
MEM_PEAK_GIB=92
. "${REPO}/ops/profiles/_flashnext.env"
# the one line _flashnext.env hardcodes to turboderp's repo: this pack is Lygodactylus's
QSE_WEIGHTS_HF=Lygodactylus/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Uncensored-exl3-4bpw
